'Let every wise-hearted man among you come, and make all that YHWH has commanded:
02230b006d	the tabernacle, its outer covering, its roof, its clasps, its boards, its bars, its pillars, and its sockets;
02230c0041	the ark, and its poles, the mercy seat, the curtain to screen it;
02230d0041	the table with its poles and all its vessels, and the show bread;
02230e0059	the lampstand also for the light, with its vessels, its lamps, and the oil for the light;
02230f0086	and the altar of incense with its poles, the anointing oil, the sweet incense, the screen for the door, at the door of the tabernacle;
0223100070	the altar of burnt offering, with its grating of bronze, its poles, and all its vessels, the basin and its base;
0223110060	the hangings of the court, its pillars, their sockets, and the screen for the gate of the court;
0223120043	the pins of the tabernacle, the pins of the court, and their cords;
02231300aa	the finely worked garments, for ministering in the holy place, the holy garments for Aaron the priest, and the garments of his sons, to minister in the priest's office.'

'When a ruler sins, and unwittingly does any one of all the things which YHWH his God has commanded not to be done, and is guilty;
0304170078	if his sin, in which he has sinned, is made known to him, he shall bring as his offering a goat, a male without blemish.
030418008d	He shall lay his hand on the head of the goat, and kill it in the place where they kill the burnt offering before YHWH. It is a sin offering.
03041900d8	The priest shall take some of the blood of the sin offering with his finger, and put it on the horns of the altar of burnt offering. He shall pour out the rest of its blood at the base of the altar of burnt offering.
03041a00b2	All its fat he shall burn on the altar, like the fat of the sacrifice of peace offerings; and the priest shall make atonement for him concerning his sin, and he will be forgiven.
03041b0085	'If anyone of the common people sins unwittingly, in doing any of the things which YHWH has commanded not to be done, and is guilty;

Drink no wine nor strong drink, you, nor your sons with you, when you go into the Tent of Meeting, that you do not die: it shall be a statute forever throughout your generations:
030a0a006e	and that you are to make a distinction between the holy and the common, and between the unclean and the clean;
030a0b006a	and that you are to teach the children of Israel all the statutes which YHWH has spoken to them by Moses.

When a man or a woman has bright spots in the skin of the body, even white bright spots;
030d2700b0	then the priest shall examine them; and look, if the bright spots on the skin of their body are a dull white, it is a harmless rash, it has broken out in the skin; he is clean.
030d280043	If a man's hair has fallen from his head, he is bald. He is clean.

The leper in whom the plague is shall wear torn clothes, and the hair of his head shall hang loose. He shall cover his upper lip, and shall cry, 'Unclean. Unclean.'
030d2e008f	All the days in which the plague is in him he shall be unclean. He is unclean. He shall dwell alone. Outside of the camp shall be his dwelling.
030d2f0067	The garment also that the plague of leprosy is in, whether it is a woolen garment, or a linen garment;

The priest shall offer the sin offering, and make atonement for him who is to be cleansed because of his uncleanness: and afterward he shall kill the burnt offering;
030e140091	and the priest shall offer the burnt offering and the meal offering on the altar. The priest shall make atonement for him, and he shall be clean.
030e1500ea	If he is poor, and can't afford so much, then he shall take one male lamb for a trespass offering to be waved, to make atonement for him, and one tenth of an ephah of fine flour mingled with oil for a meal offering, and a log of oil;

'No man of the descendants of Aaron is a leper or has an issue, may eat of the holy things, until he is clean. Whoever touches anything that is unclean by the dead, a man who has had a seminal emission;
0316050090	or whoever touches any crawling creature, whereby he may be made unclean, or a man of whom he may take uncleanness, whatever uncleanness he has;
031606008d	the person that touches any such shall be unclean until the evening, and shall not eat of the holy things, unless he bathe his body in water.
0316070070	When the sun is down, he shall be clean; and afterward he shall eat of the holy things, because it is his bread.
0316080066	That which dies of itself, or is torn by animals, he shall not eat, defiling himself by it. I am YHWH.
0316090093	'They shall therefore follow my requirements, lest they bear sin for it, and die because of it, if they profane it. I am YHWH who sanctifies them.

'If by these things you won't be reformed to me, but will walk contrary to me;
031a180060	then I will also walk contrary to you; and I will strike you, even I, seven times for your sins.
031a1900e5	I will bring a sword upon you, that will execute the vengeance of the covenant; and you will be gathered together within your cities: and I will send the pestilence among you; and you will be delivered into the hand of the enemy.
031a1a00aa	When I break your staff of bread, ten women shall bake your bread in one oven, and they shall deliver your bread again by weight: and you shall eat, and not be satisfied.
031a1b0046	'If you in spite of this won't listen to me, but walk contrary to me;

Do not cut off the tribe of the families of the Kohathites from among the Levites;
04041300bd	but thus do to them, that they may live, and not die, when they approach to the most holy things: Aaron and his sons shall go in, and appoint them everyone to his service and to his burden;
0404140050	but they shall not go in to see the sanctuary even for a moment, lest they die.

This is the law of jealousy, when a wife, being under her husband, goes astray, and is defiled;
04051e00a8	or when the spirit of jealousy comes on a man, and he is jealous of his wife; then he shall set the woman before YHWH, and the priest shall execute on her all this law.
04051f004d	The man shall be free from iniquity, and that woman shall bear her iniquity.

This is that which belongs to the Levites: from twenty-five years old and upward they shall go in to wait on the service in the work of the Tent of Meeting;
040819005e	and from the age of fifty years they shall cease waiting on the work, and shall serve no more,
04081a00a7	but shall minister with their brothers in the Tent of Meeting, to perform the duty, and shall do no service. You shall do thus to the Levites concerning their duties.

Aaron shall be gathered to his people; for he shall not enter into the land which I have given to the children of Israel, because you rebelled against my word at the waters of Meribah.
041419003f	Take Aaron and Eleazar his son, and bring them up to Mount Hor;
04141a0071	and strip Aaron of his garments, and put them on Eleazar his son: and Aaron shall be taken, and shall die there.

'In the beginnings of your months you shall offer a burnt offering to YHWH: two young bulls, and one ram, seven male lambs a year old without blemish;
041c0c00bb	and three tenth parts of an ephah of fine flour for a meal offering, mixed with oil, for each bull; and two tenth parts of fine flour for a meal offering, mixed with oil, for the one ram;
041c0d009c	and a tenth part of fine flour mixed with oil for a meal offering to every lamb; for a burnt offering of a pleasant aroma, an offering made by fire to YHWH.
041c0e00dc	Their drink offerings shall be half a hin of wine for a bull, and the third part of a hin for the ram, and the fourth part of a hin for a lamb: this is the burnt offering of every month throughout the months of the year.
041c0f0081	One male goat for a sin offering to YHWH; it shall be offered besides the continual burnt offering, and the drink offering of it.
041c10004d	'In the first month, on the fourteenth day of the month, is YHWH's Passover.

'Also in the day of the first fruits, when you offer a new meal offering to YHWH in your feast of weeks, you shall have a holy convocation; you shall do no servile work;
041c1b0079	but you shall offer a burnt offering for a pleasant aroma to YHWH: two young bulls, one ram, seven male lambs a year old;
041c1c0075	and their meal offering, fine flour mixed with oil, three tenth parts for each bull, two tenth parts for the one ram,
041c1d002f	a tenth part for every lamb of the seven lambs;
041c1e0029	one male goat, to make atonement for you.
041c1f009a	Besides the continual burnt offering, and the meal offering of it, you shall offer them (they shall be to you without blemish), and their drink offerings.
041d0100a2	'In the seventh month, on the first day of the month, you shall have a holy convocation; you shall do no servile work: it is a day of blowing of trumpets to you.

'On the tenth day of this seventh month you shall have a holy convocation; and you shall afflict your souls: you shall do no kind of work;
041d08009e	but you shall offer a burnt offering to YHWH for a pleasant aroma: one young bull, one ram, seven male lambs a year old; they shall be to you without blemish;
041d090074	and their meal offering, fine flour mixed with oil, three tenth parts for the bull, two tenth parts for the one ram,
041d0a002f	a tenth part for every lamb of the seven lambs:
041d0b00a2	one male goat for a sin offering; besides the sin offering of atonement, and the continual burnt offering, and the meal offering of it, and their drink offerings.
041d0c009b	'On the fifteenth day of the seventh month you shall have a holy convocation; you shall do no servile work, and you shall keep a feast to YHWH seven days:

'On the second day you shall offer twelve young bulls, two rams, fourteen male lambs a year old without blemish;
041d120091	and their meal offering and their drink offerings for the bulls, for the rams, and for the lambs, according to their number, after the ordinance;
041d130083	and one male goat for a sin offering; besides the continual burnt offering, and the meal offering of it, and their drink offerings.
041d14005a	'On the third day eleven bulls, two rams, fourteen male lambs a year old without blemish;

'On the fourth day ten bulls, two rams, fourteen male lambs a year old without blemish;
041d18008d	their meal offering and their drink offerings for the bulls, for the rams, and for the lambs, according to their number, after the ordinance;
041d190082	and one male goat for a sin offering; besides the continual burnt offering, the meal offering of it, and the drink offering of it.
041d1a0058	'On the fifth day nine bulls, two rams, fourteen male lambs a year old without blemish;

'On the sixth day eight bulls, two rams, fourteen male lambs a year old without blemish;
041d1e0091	and their meal offering and their drink offerings for the bulls, for the rams, and for the lambs, according to their number, after the ordinance;
041d1f0083	and one male goat for a sin offering; besides the continual burnt offering, the meal offering of it, and the drink offerings of it.
041d20005b	'On the seventh day seven bulls, two rams, fourteen male lambs a year old without blemish;

'On the eighth day you shall have a solemn assembly: you shall do no servile work;
041d24009c	but you shall offer a burnt offering, an offering made by fire, of a pleasant aroma to YHWH: one bull, one ram, seven male lambs a year old without blemish;
041d250094	their meal offering and their drink offerings for the bull, for the ram, and for the lambs, shall be according to their number, after the ordinance:
041d260086	and one male goat for a sin offering, besides the continual burnt offering, and the meal offering of it, and the drink offering of it.
041d2700d8	'You shall offer these to YHWH in your set feasts, besides your vows, and your freewill offerings, for your burnt offerings, and for your meal offerings, and for your drink offerings, and for your peace offerings.'"

Command the children of Israel, and tell them, 'When you come into the land of Canaan (this is the land that shall fall to you for an inheritance, even the land of Canaan according to its borders),
042203009c	then your south quarter shall be from the wilderness of Zin along by the side of Edom, and your south border shall be from the end of the Salt Sea eastward;
04220400d9	and your border shall turn about southward of the ascent of Akrabbim, and pass along to Zin; and the goings out of it shall be southward of Kadesh Barnea; and it shall go forth to Hazar Addar, and pass along to Azmon;
042205006e	and the border shall turn about from Azmon to the Wadi of Egypt, and the goings out of it shall be at the sea.
0422060061	'For the western border, the Great Sea shall be a border to you; this shall be your west border.

'This shall be your north border: from the Great Sea you shall mark out for you Mount Hor;
0422080065	from Mount Hor you shall mark out to Lebo Hamath; and the goings out of the border shall be at Zedad;
042209007b	and the border shall go forth to Ziphron, and the goings out of it shall be at Hazar Enan: this shall be your north border.
04220a0041	'You shall mark out your east border from Hazar Enan to Shepham;

'But if he thrust him suddenly without enmity, or hurled on him anything without lying in wait,
0423170092	or with any stone, by which a man may die, not seeing him, and cast it on him, so that he died, and he was not his enemy, neither sought his harm;
042318006d	then the congregation shall judge between the striker and the avenger of blood according to these ordinances;
042319010b	and the congregation shall deliver the manslayer out of the hand of the avenger of blood, and the congregation shall restore him to his city of refuge, where he was fled: and he shall dwell in it until the death of the high priest, who was anointed with the holy oil.
04231a0064	'But if the manslayer shall at any time go beyond the border of his city of refuge, where he flees,

Now therefore take and prepare yourselves a new cart, and two milk cows, on which there has come no yoke; and tie the cows to the cart, and take their calves from them back home;
09060800ac	and take the ark, and lay it on the cart; and put the figures of gold, which you return him for a trespass offering, in a box by its side; and send it away, that it may go.
09060900db	And watch; if it goes up by the way of its own territory to Beth Shemesh, then he has done us this great evil: but if not, then we shall know that it is not his hand that struck us; it was a chance that happened to us.

Now therefore, YHWH, God of Israel, please let your word be verified, which you spoke to your servant David my father.
0b081b0093	But will God in very deed dwell on the earth? Look, heaven and the heaven of heavens can't contain you; how much less this house that I have built.
0b081c00a8	Yet have respect for the prayer of your servant, and for his petition, YHWH my God, to listen to the cry and to the prayer which your servant prays before you this day;
0b081d00cc	that your eyes may be open toward this house night and day, even toward the place of which you have said, 'My name shall be there;' to listen to the prayer which your servant shall pray toward this place.
0b081e00b0	Listen to the petition of your servant, and of your people Israel, when they shall pray toward this place. Yes, hear in heaven, your dwelling place; and when you hear, forgive.
0b081f008e	If a man sins against his neighbor, and an oath is laid on him to cause him to swear, and he comes and swear before your altar in this house;

If your people go out to battle against their enemy, by whatever way you shall send them, and they pray to YHWH toward the city which you have chosen, and toward the house which I have built for your name;
0b082d004e	then hear in heaven their prayer and their petition, and maintain their cause.
0b082e00ca	If they sin against you (for there is no man who doesn't sin), and you are angry with them, and deliver them to the enemy, so that they carry them away captive to the land of the enemy, far off or near;
0b082f00e3	yet if they shall repent in the land where they are carried captive, and repent and make petition to you in the land of those who carried them captive, saying, 'We have sinned, and have done perversely; we have dealt wickedly;'
0b0830010e	if they return to you with all their heart and with all their soul in the land of their enemies, who carried them captive, and pray to you toward their land, which you gave to their fathers, the city which you have chosen, and the house which I have built for your name:
0b08310063	then hear their prayer and their petition in heaven, your dwelling place, and maintain their cause;
0b083200e4	and forgive your people who have sinned against you, and all their transgressions in which they have transgressed against you; and give them compassion before those who carried them captive, that they may have compassion on them
0b08330075	(for they are your people, and your inheritance, which you brought out of Egypt, from the midst of the iron furnace);
0b083400a0	that your eyes and your ears may be open to the petition of your servant, and to the petition of your people Israel, to listen to them whenever they cry to you.
0b083500b2	For you separated them from among all the peoples of the earth, to be your inheritance, as you spoke by Moses your servant, when you brought our fathers out of Egypt, Lord YHWH.

Blessed be YHWH, who has given rest to his people Israel, according to all that he promised. There has not failed one word of all his good promise, which he promised by Moses his servant.
0b0839005e	May YHWH our God be with us, as he was with our fathers. Let him not leave us, nor forsake us;
0b083a00a3	that he may incline our hearts to him, to walk in all his ways, and to keep his commandments, and his statutes, and his ordinances, which he commanded our fathers.
0b083b00d6	Let these my words, with which I have made petition before YHWH, be near to YHWH our God day and night, that he may maintain the cause of his servant, and the cause of his people Israel, as every day shall require;
0b083c0053	that all the peoples of the earth may know that YHWH, he is God. There is no other.
0b083d007f	Let your heart therefore be perfect with YHWH our God, to walk in his statutes, and to keep his commandments, as at this day."

Because I exalted you out of the dust, and made you ruler over my people Israel, and you have walked in the way of Jeroboam, and have made my people Israel to sin, to provoke me to anger with their sins;
0b1003007d	look, I will utterly sweep away Baasha and his house; and I will make your house like the house of Jeroboam the son of Nebat.
0b1004007f	The dogs will eat Baasha's descendants who die in the city; and he who dies of his in the field the birds of the sky will eat.

Because Manasseh king of Judah has done these abominations, and has done wickedly above all that the Amorites did, who were before him, and has made Judah also to sin with his idols;
0c150c0097	therefore thus says YHWH, the God of Israel, 'Look, I bring such disaster on Jerusalem and Judah, that whoever hears of it, both his ears shall tingle.
0c150d00af	I will stretch over Jerusalem the line of Samaria, and the plummet of the house of Ahab; and I will wipe Jerusalem as a man wipes a dish, wiping it and turning it upside down.
0c150e0099	I will cast off the remnant of my inheritance, and deliver them into the hand of their enemies. They will become a prey and a spoil to all their enemies;
0c150f009e	because they have done that which is evil in my sight, and have provoked me to anger, since the day their fathers came forth out of Egypt, even to this day.'

If a man sins against his neighbor and obliges him to take an oath, and he comes to take an oath before your altar in this house;
0e061700c7	then hear from heaven, and do, and judge your servants, bringing retribution to the wicked, to bring his way on his own head; and justifying the righteous, to give him according to his righteousness.
0e061800be	If your people Israel be struck down before the enemy, because they have sinned against you, and shall turn again and confess your name, and pray and make petition before you in this house;

When the sky is shut up, and there is no rain, because they have sinned against you; if they pray toward this place, and confess your name, and turn from their sin, when you punish them:
0e061b00e5	then hear in heaven, and forgive the sin of your servants, and of your people Israel, when you teach them the good way in which they should walk; and send rain on your land, which you have given to your people for an inheritance.
0e061c00d6	If there is famine in the land, if there is pestilence, if there is blight or mildew, locust or caterpillar; if their enemies besiege them in the land of their gates; whatever plague or whatever sickness there is;

Moreover concerning the foreigner, who is not of your people Israel, when he shall come from a far country for the sake of your name, for they shall hear of your great name, and your mighty hand, and your outstretched arm, when they shall come and pray toward this house,
0e06210124	then hear from heaven, even from your dwelling place, and do according to all that the foreigner calls to you for; that all the peoples of the earth may know your name, and fear you, as does your people Israel, and that they may know that this house which I have built is called by your name.
0e062200c9	If your people go out to battle against their enemies, by whatever way you shall send them, and they pray to you toward this city which you have chosen, and the house which I have built for your name;

Remember, I beg you, the word that you commanded your servant Moses, saying, 'If you trespass, I will scatter you abroad among the peoples;
10010900f8	but if you return to me, and keep my commandments and do them, though your outcasts were in the uttermost part of the heavens, yet will I gather them from there, and will bring them to the place that I have chosen, to cause my name to dwell there.'
10010a0072	Now these are your servants and your people, whom you have redeemed by your great power, and by your strong hand.

If I have withheld the poor from their desire, or have caused the eyes of the widow to fail,
121f110045	or have eaten my morsel alone, and the fatherless has not eaten of it
121f120061	(no, from my youth he grew up with me as with a father, her have I guided from my mother's womb);
121f130052	if I have seen any perish for want of clothing, or that the needy had no covering;
121f140050	if his heart hasn't blessed me, if he hasn't been warmed with my sheep's fleece;
121f150056	if I have lifted up my hand against the fatherless, because I saw my help in the gate,
121f160056	then let my shoulder fall from the shoulder blade, and my arm be broken from the bone.
121f17004f	For calamity from God is a terror to me. Because his majesty, I can do nothing.
121f180056	If I have made gold my hope, and have said to the fine gold, 'You are my confidence;'

If I have rejoiced at the destruction of him who hated me, or lifted up myself when evil found him;
121f1e004a	(yes, I have not allowed my mouth to sin by asking his life with a curse);
121f1f005e	if the men of my tent have not said, 'Who can find one who has not been filled with his meat?'
121f200059	(the foreigner has not lodged in the street, but I have opened my doors to the traveler);
121f210051	if like Adam I have covered my transgressions, by hiding my iniquity in my heart,
121f220088	because I feared the great multitude, and the contempt of families terrified me, so that I kept silence, and did not go out of the door?
121f230077	oh that I had one to hear me. (look, here is my signature, let Shaddai answer me); let the accuser write my indictment.
121f24004d	Surely I would carry it on my shoulder; and I would bind it to me as a crown.
121f250052	I would declare to him the number of my steps; as a prince would I go near to him.
121f26003f	If my land cries out against me, and its furrows weep together;
121f270057	if I have eaten its fruits without money, or have caused its owners to lose their life,
