Surely I will not come into the structure of my house, nor go up into my bed;
138404003b	I will not give sleep to my eyes, or slumber to my eyelids;
138405004b	until I find out a place for YHWH, a dwelling for the Mighty One of Jacob.

How long, you simple ones, will you love simplicity? How long will mockers delight themselves in mockery, and fools hate knowledge?
140117005e	Turn at my reproof. Look, I will pour out my spirit on you. I will make known my words to you.
1401180069	Because I have called, and you have refused; I have stretched out my hand, and no one has paid attention;
1401190043	but you have ignored all my counsel, and wanted none of my reproof;
14011a004c	I also will laugh at your disaster. I will mock when calamity overtakes you;
14011b007e	when calamity overtakes you like a storm, when your disaster comes on like a whirlwind; when distress and anguish come on you.
14011c006a	Then will they call on me, but I will not answer. They will seek me diligently, but they will not find me;
14011d0042	because they hated knowledge, and did not choose the fear of YHWH.
14011e003d	They wanted none of my counsel. They despised all my reproof.
14011f005c	Therefore they will eat of the fruit of their own way, and be filled with their own schemes.
140120005f	For the backsliding of the simple will kill them. The careless ease of fools will destroy them.
140121005a	But whoever listens to me will dwell securely, and will be at ease, without fear of harm.

I, YHWH, have called you in righteousness, and will hold your hand, and will keep you, and make you a covenant for the people, as a light for the nations;
172a070073	to open the blind eyes, to bring the prisoners out of the dungeon, and those who sit in darkness out of the prison.
172a080063	I am YHWH. That is my name. I will not give my glory to another, nor my praise to engraved images.

Listen to me, house of Jacob, and all the remnant of the house of Israel, that have been borne from their birth, that have been carried from the womb;
172e040088	and even to old age I am he, and even to gray hairs will I carry you. I have made, and I will bear; yes, I will carry, and will deliver.
172e050053	To whom will you liken me, and make me equal, and compare me, that we may be like?

I have shown myself to those who did not ask for me. I was found by those who did not seek me. I said, 'Here I am. Here I am.' to a nation that did not call on my name.
1741020093	All day long I have stretched out my hands to a disobedient and obstinate people, who walk in a way that is not good, following their own thoughts;
1741030067	a people who provoke me to my face continually as they sacrifice in gardens and burn incense on bricks;
1741040086	who sit among the graves, and lodge in the secret places; who eat pig's flesh, and the broth of abominable things is in their vessels;
174105008d	who say, 'Keep your distance, do not come near to me, for I am holier than you.' These are a smoke in my nose, a fire that burns all the day.
1741060076	Look, it is written before me: I will not keep silence, but will recompense, yes, I will recompense into their bosom,

How can you say, 'I am not defiled. I have not gone after the Baals'? See your way in the valley. Know what you have done. You are a swift dromedary traversing her ways;
18021800cc	a wild donkey used to the wilderness, that snuffs up the wind in her desire. When she is in heat, who can turn her away? All those who seek her will not weary themselves. In her month, they will find her.
180219009c	Withhold your foot from being unshod, and your throat from thirst. But you said, 'It is in vain. No, for I have loved strangers, and I will go after them.'

Thus says YHWH to me: Make bonds and bars, and put them on your neck;
181b0300e5	and send them to the king of Edom, and to the king of Moab, and to the king of the people of Ammon, and to the king of Tyre, and to the king of Sidon, by the hand of the messengers who come to Jerusalem to Zedekiah king of Judah;
181b04007b	and give them a command to their masters, saying, 'Thus says YHWH of hosts, the God of Israel, You shall tell your masters:
181b0500af	I have made the earth, the men and the animals that are on the surface of the earth, by my great power and by my outstretched arm; and I give it to whom it seems right to me.

Because you have said, 'YHWH has raised us up prophets in Babylon';
181d1000b7	thus says YHWH concerning the king who sits on the throne of David, and concerning all the people who dwell in this city, your brothers who haven't gone forth with you into captivity;
181d1100a7	thus says YHWH of hosts; 'Look, I will send on them the sword, the famine, and the pestilence, and will make them like vile figs, that can't be eaten, they are so bad.
181d120128	I will pursue after them with the sword, with the famine, and with the pestilence, and will deliver them to be tossed back and forth among all the kingdoms of the earth, to be an object of horror, and an astonishment, and a hissing, and a reproach, among all the nations where I have driven them;
